# OB-Xf for WebCLAP

OB-Xf by the Surge Synth Team, a virtual analog synthesizer continuing OB-Xd, ported to WebCLAP. This is not an
official OB-Xf release.

- OB-Xf: https://github.com/surge-synthesizer/OB-Xf (commit b08ffb6)
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-obxf.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here.

## License

The bundle as a whole is licensed under the **GNU Affero General Public License, version 3** (`LICENSE`).

OB-Xf is GPL-3.0-or-later (`licenses/GPL-3.0.txt`). Both modules contain the JUCE framework (the DSP module its
GUI-free part), used under the AGPL-3.0, so `module.wasm` and `ui/ui.wasm` are AGPL-3.0. GPL-3.0 section 13
permits the combination.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied
warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the licenses for details.

